{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1, confirmed)\n\nRoot cause: write/remove key asymmetry in the link store API.\n\n- WRITE is relation-scoped: graph/_links.py::add_dependency is idempotent per (target_id, relation) ('if a net-active LINK with the same (target_id, relation) already exists' — docstring), so one ordered pair can hold e.g. blocks AND relates_to simultaneously.\n- REMOVE is pair-scoped: _commands/unlink.py::_get_link_info returns 'the most recent net-active link for target' (no relation key), and rebar.unlink/unlink_core expose no relation parameter.\n- Consequence: rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py::_inbound_unlink_one (guard G5, change 1276 / bug 2b16) asks _get_link_info what a pair-scoped unlink WOULD remove and declines with a WARNING when that relation differs from the relation whose peer link vanished. Correct fail-safe direction, but the decline is permanent: inbound_differ._diff_link_removals_inbound re-emits the removal every pass and G5 re-declines it, so the two systems never converge for a double-related pair, with no operator-visible signal beyond a log line.\n\nLegitimacy: defect (silent non-convergence of the reconciler's inbound removal contract), confirmed live by the coexistence of two relations per pair (idempotency key in add_dependency) — G5 is not dead code. Fix design ratified by the operator (see previous comment). Caller sweep: _inbound_unlink_one is the only G5 caller; rebar.unlink callers (CLI dispatcher, MCP unlink_tickets, reconciler) all pass no relation and keep identical behavior under the optional-arg extension."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785860631955731001,"uuid":"27588409-6c32-44c7-bdf2-97a712f5adf7"}